      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1309351704">
          <groundspeak:date>2025-07-08T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP755 CBP7 [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure exactly where my travels will lead today, but this morning I was around here, mainly DNFing caches (which I seem to do a lot in the woods), but I was also able to find this. It’s in pretty good shape and I actually spotted it very quickly. Thanks! &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="729284382">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-10-21T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="5323897">brendan714</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP755 CBP7

N 51° 05.756 W 114° 14.057&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I searched for this cap for a couple minutes at an obvious spot before noticing some flagging.  Once I re-directed my search near the flagging, the cap was soon (FOUND).  A nice hunt, thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="699687189">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="51.095933" lon="-114.234317" />
          <groundspeak:date>2017-07-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1074559">van der Decken</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP755 - CBP7

Elev. 1120 metres&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hot enough for ya?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It might not have been the brightest idea I've had all week. Biking out to the far west end of town on the hottest day of the year, I mean. There &lt;em&gt;was&lt;/em&gt; a breeze, which helped a bit at times. But there's no getting around it; it was a hot one out there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There wasn't a whole lot of folk out on the pathways (go figure) but the Bow river was quite busy. All kinds of folk were floating down it. Some of the watercraft were suited for a fast moving river but many of them shouldn't have been on anything rougher than a backyard pool. Life preservers? Don't make me laugh. Snort...&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I knew from reading previous finds that this cap was throwing curve balls. And even though I'd read the hint, &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; there was flagging right over the cap, it still took a bit to spot it. The flagging has been there for awhile and has faded quite a bit and I didn't even see it at first. And even after I saw the flagging (and it was &lt;em&gt;right&lt;/em&gt; over the cap too), I still didn't see the cap until I moved to a different angle and got the compass out.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It was the heat, you see. Right.... 😉&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ground level cap is in very good shape. It blends in amazingly well. Thanks for the bike-able brass cap, outforthehunt! (FOUND)&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
